hey everyone I'm Rob and welcome to my  tutorial on how to make an origami  flapping bird in this tutorial I will  teach you how to make the bird using a  regular sheet of printer paper making  the bird is very similar to making the  origami crane but there are fewer folds  involved with making the bird give you  links to my other origami tutorials  please scroll down to the right and view  series playlist or you can visit my  channel by clicking on my name down to  the right as well once on my channel  simply click on the origami crane in my  channel banner to view all of my other  origami tutorials in order to make the  bird and also the crane we need to first  learn how to make bird base if you know  how to make the bird base I'll put a  small subtitle down here letting you  know where you could fast forward to in  the tutorial if you don't know how to  make the bird base that's what we're  going to learn how to do now to convert  your printer paper into a square take  one corner and fold it down to the  opposite side making sure that this edge  is aligned with the side edge make a  crease and then you could remove the  excess paper when you do so you'll have  a piece of paper that looks like this  and when you open it you'll notice you  now have a diagonal fold now we're going  to take the top of the paper and fold it  down in half so that it meets the bottom  end of the paper make a crease and then  when you open it you'll see you now have  a horizontal fold now we're going to  fold the paper in half going this way  take the top half again and fold it down  to the bottom half make another crease  so now when you open up the paper you'll  notice you now have a cross in the paper  and also a diagonal fold we want to take  the paper and fold it in half on the  diagonal fold make sure it's nice and  flat then we lift up the first layer of  paper and we're going to tuck this  corner in down towards the bottom in the  middle of the paper so tuck the corner  in and then we make really good creases  on those new folds which we just created  so now we want to take the left side of  the paper and tuck this corner and as  well so tuck it in and then we want to  flatten the entire structure out also so  make good creases all throughout the  paper now you should have a diamond  structure that looks just like this if  you made really good creases when you  were tucking in the corners then you  should notice a faint line that runs  vertically down the center of the  diamond if you don't notice the line  then you could take the entire diamond  and fold it in half and then make a  crease down the edge then you should  notice that you have a vertical line  what we're going to be doing in this  step is folding each of these four flaps  inwards towards the center of that line  so that this edge on the bottom aligns  with that vertical line so you want to  fold each of the flaps inwards just like  that and then make a crease so you  should have something that looks like  that and you want to do the same with  the remaining three flaps fold it  inwards and make a crease flip it over  and do the same in order to complete the  bird base we must now perform what is  known as the petal fold which is the  trickiest fold of making the bird base  I'm going to show you some ways now that  we can make the folding a little bit  easier one of the things you could do is  to take the tip of this kite and we're  going to fold it straight down so that  it folds along this edge here made by  these two flaps so you want to fold it  straight down along that edge and then  you make a crease unfold it flip the  model over and do the exact same thing  on this side  okay so now another thing you could do  is as you'll notice these flaps are  folded this way if we take each of these  flaps and fold them backwards on that  fold flip the model over do the same  thing on this side so fold it backwards  unfold it and just fold it backwards on  that line on that crease which we made  that will also make the petal fold a  little bit easier so now we could lay  the model flat on the table we're going  to lift up this first layer of paper and  you want to just kind of tug on it as  you'll see it might not want to fold  that way just kind of take your thumb  and push on those creases which were  made so tug upwards and you'll see these  edges will now go towards the center  take both of your hands and just push  gently on it and make good creases along  the outside of the petal fold so you  should have something that looks like  this flip the model over and do the  exact same thing lift up the first layer  of paper push outwards tug up on it and  then you want to just make the model  nice and flat by making really good  creases on the outside now that you've  completed the bird base just make sure  you're holding it so that these two  bottom halves are the ones that are  separate and the top should be solid  we're going to go on to make the head  and tail and also fold the wings down to  complete the bird turn the model on the  side and open up these two side flaps  we're then going to fold the point here  upwards all the way and then we're going  to close the two flaps on it pull the  point outwards and then we just want to  make sure that this is folded in half  nicely so just crease it along the edge  there so now you want to pull this point  outwards until this edge is aligned with  this edge here just pull it out to right  about there make a crease along the  bottom  and you should have something that looks  like this do the same with the left side  open up these two flaps fold the point  upwards close the flaps pull this out  make sure it's creased in half and then  you want to pull it out - right about  there make a crease along the bottom  okay so now all we have to do is to make  the head and to fold down the wings I'm  going to make the right side the head  and the left side is going to be the  tail so to make the head just open up  this point here in the middle push down  on the top of it and then just pinch the  top to make a crease then we're going to  be folding the wings towards the head  the tip of it is going to be more  towards the head I've made a line here  to show you exactly where there needs to  be folded from here down to here so you  want to fold it along that line and then  you want to make a crease flip the model  over and now you can kind of line this  wing up with the other wing so fold it  down and then make another crease then  you can just lift the wings up a little  bit and to make a stand we need to just  take these points and fold them outwards  and then to make it flap all you need to  do is to hold it here by the neck and  then just pull on the tail if it if it  seems like it's going to rip all you  need to do is just kind of pull outwards  on this a little bit like I showed you  just fold outwards and then it shouldn't  it should be fine just hold on it and  there you go you have your flapping bird  so I hope you guys enjoy the tutorial  and be sure to comment rate and  subscribe I'm thinking of making an  origami ring tutorial out of a dollar  bill so let me know what you think of  that and thanks for watching
 

